---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="AI & automation notice"
  description="How OriginsLynk uses AI and automation, where human review remains required, and which results are not guaranteed."
>
  <section class="section-cream page-hero">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">AI &amp; automation notice</p>
      <h1>Useful systems still need defined limits.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        OriginsLynk may use selected AI services, automation platforms, integrations, and
        infrastructure to perform the work described in an approved workflow. The exact tools
        depend on compatibility, security, availability, and the client’s requirements.
      </p>
      <p class="small muted updated">Effective August 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container container-narrow legal-copy">
      <article>
        <h2>What these systems may do</h2>
        <p>
          Approved workflows may organize information, classify routine inputs, prepare drafts,
          summarize material, create reports, schedule review-ready work, route exceptions, or
          perform other specifically documented steps. Every workflow has a defined trigger,
          source boundary, output, owner, approval point, and failure path before production use.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>AI can be wrong</h2>
        <p>
          AI-generated content and automated decisions may be incomplete, inaccurate, biased,
          delayed, or unsuitable for the intended situation. Testing reduces known risks but
          does not make a system infallible. Important facts, calculations, commitments, and
          customer-facing outputs must be reviewed by the designated person.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>Human approval remains the default</h2>
        <p>
          Consequential messages, publication, money movement, signatures, deletion, permanent
          record changes, and business commitments remain human-approved unless a signed
          workflow specification expressly defines a narrower authorized process and its
          safeguards. Clients remain responsible for deciding whether an output is used.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>Operating responsibility depends on the service</h2>
        <p>
          Tier 1 and Tier 2 are client-operated and include no OriginsLynk monitoring or
          recurring maintenance. Tier 3 includes only the monitoring, maintenance, backup, and
          response duties stated in the managed-service agreement. No tier guarantees
          uninterrupted availability or detection of every possible failure.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>Third-party providers and charges</h2>
        <p>
          Connected providers may process approved workflow information under their own terms
          and may change, restrict, suspend, or discontinue features. Required client-owned
          subscriptions, API usage, message fees, storage, and other provider charges are
          separate unless the written proposal states otherwise. Relevant providers are
          disclosed during proposal and onboarding.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>Data and credentials</h2>
        <p>
          OriginsLynk requests the minimum information and access needed for an approved
          workflow. Clients enter credentials through the approved account or credential store;
          passwords and access codes should never be sent through the public form or ordinary
          email. See the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a> and the
          <a href="/trust#data-handling">Trust &amp; Safety</a> page for more detail.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>High-risk work is excluded by default</h2>
        <p>
          Standard OriginsLynk services are not intended for medical diagnosis or treatment,
          legal advice, regulated financial or credit decisions, autonomous employment or
          insurance decisions, emergency response, surveillance, payment-card storage, or
          other safety-critical or regulated uses. Such requests require separate written
          assessment and may be declined.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>No guaranteed business outcome</h2>
        <p>
          Examples and estimates illustrate possible workflow improvements. OriginsLynk does
          not guarantee revenue, leads, savings, productivity, accuracy, compatibility, or a
          particular business result. Actual results depend on the process, source data, client
          review, staff adoption, connected services, and operating conditions.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-hero h1 { max-width: 17ch; }
  .page-hero .lede { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
  .updated { margin-top: var(--space-4); }
  .legal-copy { display: grid; gap: var(--space-7); }
  .legal-copy article { padding-top: var(--space-5); border-top: var(--border-thin) solid var(--rule-strong); }
  .legal-copy h2 { font-size: var(--text-xl); }
  .legal-copy p { margin-top: var(--space-4); color: var(--ink-muted); }
</style>
